# The welcome window on a phone (Hameron, Pixel, Android 11-12): the screen is 1080 px wide and Android's UI scale ran
# at 300 %, so the fixed 500 dp window was wider than the screen and its X and Close button were off it. The window
# stays inside the 3D view's area, at the phone's portrait size and at a desktop scale, and its X closes it.
# CMake runs this at 1080x2400.
ui_scale 300
run new_sphere subdivisions=3
key f3
type "##Command palette" "welcome"
key enter
wait_idle 10
expect_value welcome_open == 1
expect_value welcome_outside_px == 0
shot welcome-phone-300
ui_scale 100
wait_idle 10
expect_value welcome_outside_px == 0
shot welcome-phone-100
ui_scale 300
wait_idle 10
expect_value welcome_outside_px == 0
click "Close##welcome"
expect_value welcome_open == 0
